@page "/docs/api-reference/discovery"
@layout DocsLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Discovery — Vaultex API</PageTitle>

<div class="docs-eyebrow">API reference</div>
<h1>Discovery</h1>
<p class="docs-lead">
    OIDC clients auto-configure themselves by reading the discovery document. You almost never call
    these endpoints by hand &mdash; SDKs do it for you.
</p>

<h2 id="metadata">OpenID configuration</h2>
<div class="docs-endpoint">
    <span class="docs-method docs-method--get">GET</span>
    <span>/.well-known/openid-configuration</span>
</div>

<p>Returns a JSON document listing every endpoint, supported scope, and supported response type.</p>

<h3>Example response</h3>
<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">JSON</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>{
  "issuer":                "https://auth.vaultex.io",
  "authorization_endpoint": "https://auth.vaultex.io/connect/authorize",
  "token_endpoint":         "https://auth.vaultex.io/connect/token",
  "userinfo_endpoint":      "https://auth.vaultex.io/connect/userinfo",
  "end_session_endpoint":   "https://auth.vaultex.io/connect/logout",
  "revocation_endpoint":    "https://auth.vaultex.io/connect/revocation",
  "jwks_uri":               "https://auth.vaultex.io/.well-known/jwks",
  "response_types_supported": ["code", "id_token", "code id_token"],
  "grant_types_supported":    ["authorization_code", "refresh_token"],
  "scopes_supported":         ["openid", "profile", "email", "roles", "offline_access"],
  "code_challenge_methods_supported": ["S256"],
  "id_token_signing_alg_values_supported": ["RS256"]
}</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="jwks">JSON Web Key Set</h2>
<div class="docs-endpoint">
    <span class="docs-method docs-method--get">GET</span>
    <span>/.well-known/jwks</span>
</div>

<p>Returns the public keys used to sign tokens. APIs cache this document and use it to verify incoming JWT signatures.</p>

<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">JSON</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>{
  "keys": [{
    "kty": "RSA",
    "use": "sig",
    "kid": "kid-2026-05",
    "alg": "RS256",
    "n":   "v8h...",
    "e":   "AQAB"
  }]
}</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="docs-callout docs-callout--info">
    <span class="docs-callout-icon">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M11 7h2v2h-2zm0 4h2v6h-2zm1-9C6.48 2 2 6.48 2 12s4.48 10 10 10 10-4.48 10-10S17.52 2 12 2z"/></svg>
    </span>
    <div class="docs-callout-body">
        <div class="docs-callout-title">Key rotation</div>
        <p>Vaultex rotates signing keys periodically. The JWKS endpoint always returns the current set; cache it for at most 24 hours.</p>
    </div>
</div>

